{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8s4tFFyh9E9Ndz62mbJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the audit to `ANSWER.md`. One thing first: your `20261010040000_normal_forms.sql` migration already made every fix in the guide. So the report covers only what's still not in 3NF, which is mostly things added after that migration or missed by it.\n\nI had no database access, so I didn't count how many live rows break each rule. Each finding in the file comes with a read-only SQL query for that count.\n\n**Derived values stored next to their source (the problem the guide fixed on `drafts`, back again):**\n- **`model_calls`:** `tokens_in`, `tokens_out` and `cost_usd` are just parts of `usage`, but the app writes them separately, so nothing keeps them equal.\n- **`code_questions.cost_usd`:** a copy of `usage.cost_usd`. The success path and the failure path also calculate it from different sources, so they can disagree.\n- **`voice_samples.quality`:** a copy of `scores.quality`. Rule-rejected rows already disagree: `quality = 0` with `scores = null`.\n- **`drafts.posted_by` / `posted_at`:** always equal to `decided_by` / `decided_at` when the outcome is \"posted\", and null otherwise.\n\n**Columns that copy a parent row:**\n- **`touches.platform`:** comes from the item, but the foreign key doesn't check it. Incoming touches also copy the item's text, url, kind and time.\n- **`ideas.quote`:** a copy of the first `idea_items.quote`.\n- **`document_chunks.title`:** has the document's title built into it (\"Doc › Section\"), and the code splits it apart again.\n- **`document_chunks.published_at` / `published_precision`:** in practice just the document's values. Dating each chunk separately isn't implemented, even though that's why the columns were kept.\n- **`projects.github_board_id` / `title`:** determined by the board's owner and number.\n- **`items.my_post`:** the same article snapshot repeated on every comment under that post.\n- **`voice_samples` from posted replies:** copies of the draft. The only link back is the text `'draft:<uuid>'`, not a real foreign key.\n- **Per-project copies of platform data (2NF):** a person's profile on `identities` is stored once per project. I recommend keeping this on purpose, because row-level security filters by project, but writing that decision down.\n\nThe file also lists smaller points (`people.avatar_url` as a cache, GitHub issue state, the unused `settings.draft_model`, `item_themes` having no project check) and a suggested order for fixing everything. I didn't write any migrations or change any code."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5955,"cache_read_input_tokens":86768,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5955},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6221fcd9-ed61-4953-af7a-6a05e2b1ef0e","uuid":"bfc4c576-3497-4386-bcc0-1e42a569b718","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:50:45.659Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8s4sydEnNhkmK64g9bx"}
